      "mergedPostDetails": "Thank you for your continued work on the development and maintenance of VRChat.\n\nThere is a noticeable issue where the UI pointer begins to jitter severely as the player moves away from the world origin (0,0,0).\n\nPreviously, such behavior would only occur at very large distances (around 2000 m or more), but recently (within the past few months), the problem now appears as close as about 200 m from the origin.\n\nThis behavior seems related to floating-point precision errors in Unity.\n\nHowever, the effect has become roughly ten times more sensitive than before, occurring at distances where precision errors should normally be negligible.\n\nIn larger worlds, this issue makes UI interaction nearly impossible due to how unstable the pointer becomes.\n\nA test world is available here:\n\n🔗 https://vrch.at/w98rrmkv\n\nA video demonstrating the issue is also attached.\n\nIt shows pointer behavior at the following distances from the origin:\n\nNear origin – stable (normal)\n\nX = 200 m – visible jitter begins\n\nX = 500 m – severe jitter, difficult to interact\n\nX = 1000 m – pointer becomes completely unstable, UI interaction impossible\n\nThe issue is reproducible across multiple environments.\n\nThank you for taking the time to look into this.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "UI pointer becomes extremely jittery when moving away from the world origin",
