      "reactions": null,
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5f7b354f356ab03255ef6246|full_name} On large worlds, we often set the reference camera to near clip values above 0.01 to get a correct far clip plane that doesn't break geometry or shaders in some cases (especially in Unity 2022, where clear-on-skybox ceases to function at 30 km). The Forced Near Distance setting completely overrides the world settings to \"accommodate\" 0.001 m near clip on the ref camera, which destroys the far clip setting and anything that depends on it. Completely trashes flight worlds especially where the far clip needs to be higher than 250000 m to not look like your just flying into nothing. I believe that the most appropriate solution is for VRChat to add an option to the world settings on the site to \"Disable Forced Near Distance for This World\", since this would be very easy for them to implement and not require any action on the part of players, nor would it mess with the actual use cases of Forced Near Distance in the slightest.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
